# Games Plan Documents — Sync Rule

Two planning projects exist as documentation only. When implementation begins, or when
any new information changes an assumption, **the documents must be updated in the same
piece of work as the code.**

| Folder | Covers |
|---|---|
| `New games plan/` | Stage 0 defect fixes, then the in-house game-module architecture |
| `External game plans/` | Integrating games from a third-party skill-game provider |

## THE SCENARIO IS DECIDED - EXTERNAL-FIRST (owner, 2 September 2026, amended 5 September)

**Provider games are the route. The active programme is `External game plans/` and its
X0-X12 phases**, now including **X4a**. Read `External game plans/PROGRESS.md` first.

**This heading used to read EXTERNAL-ONLY and say "no in-house game is built". That sentence
is now false**, and the amendment is recorded here rather than by rewriting the 2 September
decision, because a reversed direction is exactly the fact a new chat needs. On **5 September
2026** the owner answered open question 10 yes: the platform **is** building one game of its
own, as phase **X4a** (`21`), where it doubles as the reference implementation that proves the
provider seam. What survives of the original decision is the important part - the programme is
still external-**first**, and `New games plan` P2's in-house Trivia game is still not being
built. **The precise distinction, because it is load-bearing:** there is no in-house game
*module*, because X4a is a provider game that happens to be ours and arrives through the seam
that already exists. So "no in-house game module" is right; "no in-house game" is wrong.

| Scenario | Meaning | Chapters | Programme | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **External-first** | Provider games are the route. **One in-house game is built as a hedge** (X4a, 5 Sep 2026), speaking the provider protocol rather than as a game module | `01`-`09` **and** `10`-`21` | X0-X12 incl. **X4a**, **26.5-35 weeks** | **CHOSEN** |
| **Add-on** | The `New games plan` is delivered too. External games are an addition | `01`-`09` | E1-E9, 7.5-8 weeks on top of the foundation | **Not pursued.** Kept only so E-phase references resolve |

Chapters `10`-`20` exist because `01`-`09` delegated the foundation and every
platform-wide change (admin, navigation, wording, flags, catalogue, risks, rollout) to the
`New games plan`. That plan is not being delivered, so the dependency did not disappear -
it moved into `External game plans/`, and `10`-`20` own it.

**What the decision does to the `New games plan` folder**, because "superseded" is too
blunt: **Stage 0 / `00a` is fully active and unchanged** - it is X0, a prerequisite in
every scenario, and the work currently awaiting owner test. **P1 survives as X1**, same
seams, delivered from `External game plans/11`. **P2, the in-house Trivia game, is not
being built.** **P3-P7 are delivered as X6-X11.** The chapters remain valuable as analysis
of the live codebase, and `15-platform-transformation-and-gaps.md` is still the record of
the games-first direction.

**The finding to keep repeating, because the intuition is wrong:** external-only is **not
cheaper**, it is broader. Dropping an in-house game saves ~3.5 weeks; a correct provider
integration costs ~7; all the platform work is identical. The prize is a catalogue and no
content burden, not a saving. Do not let a summary anywhere imply otherwise.

**The consequence of the decision that must stay visible:** there is now **no in-house
game to fall back on**. If the provider search or the pricing fails, the platform will
have funded the whole foundation, admin and player programme and still have one game. That
is risk **X8**, and it is why open question 10 - a small in-house hedge game - moved
*forward* to before X4 rather than away.

### Two owner instructions that came with the decision

Both change the order rather than the contents, and both are load-bearing.

- **Admin first.** An operator must be able to register a provider, sync a catalogue and
  create a non-trading contest before any player screen has something real to render. The
  admin app is also a separate process with no player traffic, so it is the safe place to
  be wrong. **It does not mean X6 moves in front of X1-X5** - a contest must exist before
  it can be administered. In practice it means X6 and X6.5 complete *before* X7 begins.
- **One step at a time, without breaking the running app.** Every phase additive and
  flag-gated, trading pinned by the regression test in `11`, and the rule that **no phase
  may require a simultaneous change to trading in order to be correct.** If one appears
  to, the seam in `11` is wrong and that is the thing to fix.

